  "id": "pupil",
  "term": "pupil",
  "definition": "In cognition research, the pupil is the opening in the eye whose dilation can be measured as an objective, real-time indicator linked to the mental effort involved in tasks such as word processing and lexical access. Changes in pupil size are studied with pupillometry, although exactly what these responses reflect during word processing is not yet fully settled.",
